.SS "struct \fBstumpless_target\fP * stumpless_open_socket_target (const char * name, const char * local_socket)"

.PP
Opens a socket target\&. \fBThread Safety: MT-Safe race:name race:local_socket\fP This function is thread safe, of course assuming that the target name and socket name are not modified by any other threads during execution\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe heap\fP This function is not safe to call from signal handlers due to the use of memory allocation functions\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe heap\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, as the memory allocation function may not be AC-Safe itself\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIname\fP The name of the socket target, and the socket to send logs to\&.
.br
\fIlocal_socket\fP The name of the Unix domain socket to connect from\&. This can be set to NULL if you'd like to use the default name of stumpless-socket\&. If abstract socket names are supported, then this name will be abstract and therefore not appear in the filesystem\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The opened target if no error is encountered\&. In the event of an error, NULL is returned and an error code is set appropriately\&. 
.RE
.PP

